ource.com/335963 Commit-Ready: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Andrey Petrov &lt;andrey.petrov@intel.com&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="335963" owner_email="andrey.petrov@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/63/335963/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.02" change_id="I8dec768cf8763dbe235f0ba1339079ebc49cbd9a" commit="84406e57c2ed9cbae6a98fb83d27d15c452f0246" commit_message="UPSTREAM: arch/x86: Reserve space for stack in CAR layout  Some platforms may want to use C code in bootblock so they need writable memory and CAR can be used for it. This change reserves memory in CAR that can be used by bootblock and other CAR stages.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:51844 BRANCH=none TEST=none yet, the full stack of patches boots to payload on APLK  Change-Id: I8dec768cf8763dbe235f0ba1339079ebc49cbd9a Signed-off-by: Andrey Petrov &lt;andrey.petrov@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://review.coreboot.org/13640 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: build bot (Jenkins) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/335964 Commit-Ready: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="335964" owner_email="andrey.petrov@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/64/335964/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.02" change_id="Ifc705016290807c49dc8c49b581864cac2ad3f80" commit="4df2b1bc38400a41ac7cabfa95dffeb972eeb80f" commit_message="UPSTREAM: arch/x86: Allow bootblock code to use CAR_GLOBAL variables  Since cbmem is not initialized in bootblock, CAR_GLOBAL variables can only be acc